VeridianOS: fix unused-parameter warnings in the brightness controllers

GCC reported -Wunused-parameter in daemon/controllers:

- ddcutildisplay.cpp, DDCutilDisplay::setBrightness() ('value',
  'allowAnimations') and BrightnessWorker::ddcSetBrightness() ('value',
  'display'): the bodies are compiled only with WITH_DDCUTIL, which this
  build does not define. Parameters used inside that block are marked
  [[maybe_unused]]; 'allowAnimations' is not used on either path (DDC/CI
  brightness is not animated) and is left unnamed.
- kwinbrightness.cpp, KWinDisplayBrightness::setBrightness()
  ('allowAnimations'): the requested brightness is applied through a KWin
  output configuration, which takes no animation flag; the parameter is
  left unnamed.

Behaviour is unchanged.

diff -ru a/daemon/controllers/ddcutildisplay.cpp b/daemon/controllers/ddcutildisplay.cpp
--- a/daemon/controllers/ddcutildisplay.cpp	2026-10-08 17:15:45.064974113 -0400
+++ b/daemon/controllers/ddcutildisplay.cpp	2026-10-08 17:16:04.447129974 -0400
@@ -192,7 +192,7 @@
     Q_EMIT retryInitFinished(m_supportsBrightness);
 }
 
-void DDCutilDisplay::setBrightness(int value, bool allowAnimations)
+void DDCutilDisplay::setBrightness([[maybe_unused]] int value, bool /*allowAnimations*/)
 {
 #ifdef WITH_DDCUTIL
     if (m_supportsBrightness) {
@@ -226,7 +226,7 @@
     }
 }
 
-void BrightnessWorker::ddcSetBrightness(int value, DDCutilDisplay *display)
+void BrightnessWorker::ddcSetBrightness([[maybe_unused]] int value, [[maybe_unused]] DDCutilDisplay *display)
 {
 #ifdef WITH_DDCUTIL
     qCDebug(POWERDEVIL) << "[DDCutilDisplay]:" << display->m_label << "setting brightness to" << value << "with temporary display handle";
